invariant: INV-16
file: handshake_flight.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh
reason: the client hashes the ClientHello it built under a value with every
  bit set, where it must hand on the session's ch_cfg.cpu. A client whose
  caller never stated the SHA-256 instructions then runs them over its
  transcript, and on a CPU without them it dies of SIGILL before its
  first byte leaves (docs/decisions.md 93). The transcript hash is the
  same, so every handshake on a CPU with the instructions still passes.
  The script runs whole QUIC and TCP handshakes whose ends leave the bit
  clear under qemu-x86_64 on a model without the SHA extensions, where
  the first such instruction ends the process. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    TRANSCRIPT_UPDATE_CPU(t->cfg.cpu, &t->transcript, out, n);
--- new
    TRANSCRIPT_UPDATE_CPU(~0U, &t->transcript, out, n);
